  "prefLabel": "He-M 306.07 Decision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 306.07 Decision.\n\n(a) Within 2 business days of the hearing, the presiding officer shall issue a written decision.\n\n(b) The presiding officer shall authorize treatment if the presiding officer determines that the licensed practitioner demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence the criteria for emergency treatment as set forth in He-M 306.04.\n\n(c) The presiding officer shall not dismiss a petition for treatment of a medical emergency solely on the basis of the lack of psychiatric emergency.\n\n(d) The treatment authorized shall be the treatment proposed in the written request for authorization unless, during the course of testimony, the licensed practitioner recommends an amendment to the proposed treatment.\n\nSource. #3096, eff 8-19-85; EXPIRED: 8-19-91\n\nNew. #4708, eff 12-1-89, EXPIRED: 12-1-95\n\nNew. #7133, eff 11-23-99; ss by #7559, eff 9-25-01; ss by #9520, eff 8-4-09, EXPIRED: 8-4-18\n\nNew. #13035, EMERGENCY, eff 4-14-20, EXPIRES: 10-11-20; ss by #13108, eff 9-22-20; ss by #14637, eff 6-26-26, EXPIRES: 6-26-36 (formerly He-M 306.06)",
